codex
The concurrency dump identifies the blocker precisely: run 16 is stuck in `LibSSH2AdapterIntegrationTests.automaticKeepaliveSurvivesLongRekey()`, where `transport.close()` waits on teardown while both teardown and timeout paths depend on `ManualFixtureClock`; the automatic keepalive failure path is concurrently waiting on the same teardown. This is a deterministic manual-clock/lifecycle deadlock in the same real-sshd suite. Because the AC requires 20 consecutive unfiltered runs, the review cannot accept the current handoff even though the originally named cancellation test itself is improved. I’m cleaning up only the reviewer-created stuck process, then I’ll attach the stack-backed verdict and route it to development.
